// ROTN GAP-4 live repro -- SPEND-CAP policy, PLUS-CURRENT variant (AgentCore namespace).
//
// Live AgentCore's temporal window is NON-reflexive: the `sum over ::request`
// does NOT include the current in-flight request being decided (unlike the
// formal spec, where the window IS reflexive — guide/08 §6: evaluation at
// position i reads only positions j <= i, including the current event; §6.1
// observe-before-decide; guide/04 (04-temporal-expressions.md) "Evaluation
// semantics": decision at timepoint i reads history 0..=i).  So the
// plain `sum <= 200` form degenerates to "prior sum <= 200" and admits an
// off-by-one-request overshoot ($300 over the $200 cap).
//
// This variant compensates with the `+ context.input.amount` idiom (the
// refund_budget_settled_plus_current shape): it charges the CURRENT request
// against the cap explicitly, so the guard is (prior authorized sum) + current
// <= 200.  Expected live behavior (cap = 200, three parallel $100 fires):
//   if the engine serializes decisions : fire#1 100<=200 ADMIT, fire#2 200<=200
//     ADMIT, fire#3 300>200 DENY  -> cap enforced
//   if the engine races decisions      : all three read prior-sum 0 -> 3 ADMIT,
//     $300  -> a TOCTOU race no sum-policy can close
// {{GATEWAY_ARN}} is replaced with the real gateway ARN at deploy time.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"TransferTarget___transfer",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"{{GATEWAY_ARN}}"
)
when temporal {
    (sum amt for (amt: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (
            AgentCore::Action::"TransferTarget___transfer"::request{
                eventResource: resource,
                input.amount: amt
            } && tp(t)
        )
    )) + context.input.amount <= 200
};